  "worked_solution": "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (2{x}^{3})|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(2)^{3}-2(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =6 \\\\ 6{c}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ c & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
